{"seq":14,"slug":"ecology","title":"生态学","stage":"DONE","category":"biology-life-science","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology","rating":{"composite":4.02,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.2,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 生态学知识中心\n\n## 概述\n\n生态学（Ecology）是研究生物体与其环境之间相互关系的科学。这门学科涵盖从个体到生物圈的多个组织层次，揭示生命系统如何在复杂的物理和生物环境中运作、持续和演变。作为生物学的核心分支之一，生态学为理解生物多样性、生态系统功能以及人类活动对自然界的影响提供了理论框架。\n\n本知识中心系统梳理生态学的核心概念与前沿进展，从基础原理到应用实践，帮助读者建立完整的生态学认知体系。\n\n## 学习路径\n\n本中心按照从基础到应用的逻辑组织为四大章节：\n\n### 第一章：生态学基础（Foundations）\n\n建立生态系统的基本概念框架，掌握能量流动与物质循环两大驱动过程。这是理解所有高层次生态学现象的基石。\n\n### 第二章：种群生态学（Population Ecology）\n\n聚焦种群层面的动态过程，包括种群增长模型、物种间相互作用以及集合种群理论。理解种群如何在时间和空间中变化是连接个体与群落的关键桥梁。\n\n### 第三章：群落生态学（Community Ecology）\n\n探讨多物种共存的格局与机制，包括生物多样性度量、群落演替与干扰动态以及食物网结构。群落层面的研究揭示了物种多样性维持的机制。\n\n### 第四章：应用生态学（Applied Ecology）\n\n将生态学理论应用于保护实践，涵盖保护生物学、恢复生态学和气候变化生态效应。这些知识对于应对当今全球环境挑战至关重要。\n\n## 先修知识\n\n- 基础生物学概念（细胞、有机体、物种）\n- 基本化学知识（元素循环、化学反应）\n- 基础数学（指数增长、微分方程基本概念）\n- 推荐先学习 [进化生物学](../03_evolutionary-biology/INDEX.md) 的基本概念\n\n## 章节关联\n\n本中心各章节之间存在紧密的逻辑联系：每一层次的理解都建立在前一层次的基础之上——从能量/物质的基础概念，到种群层面的增长与互作，再到群落层面的多样性与网络结构，最终到保护与恢复的应用实践。建议按顺序学习，同时各章节内的文档之间也存在大量交叉引用，鼓励在不同主题间建立联系。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"生态学基础","docCount":3,"url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"ecosystem-concepts","title":"生态系统基本概念","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/foundations/ecosystem-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"energy-flow-trophic-levels","title":"能量流动与营养级","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/foundations/energy-flow-trophic-levels"},{"seq":3,"slug":"nutrient-cycling","title":"物质循环","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/foundations/nutrient-cycling"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"population-ecology","title":"种群生态学","docCount":3,"url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/population-ecology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"population-dynamics","title":"种群动态","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/population-ecology/population-dynamics"},{"seq":2,"slug":"species-interactions","title":"物种间相互作用","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/population-ecology/species-interactions"},{"seq":3,"slug":"metapopulation-theory","title":"集合种群理论","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/population-ecology/metapopulation-theory"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"community-ecology","title":"群落生态学","docCount":3,"url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/community-ecology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"biodiversity-metrics","title":"生物多样性度量","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/community-ecology/biodiversity-metrics"},{"seq":2,"slug":"succession-disturbance","title":"群落演替与干扰动态","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/community-ecology/succession-disturbance"},{"seq":3,"slug":"food-webs-networks","title":"食物网与生态网络","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/community-ecology/food-webs-networks"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"applied-ecology","title":"应用生态学","docCount":3,"url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/applied-ecology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"conservation-biology","title":"保护生物学","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/applied-ecology/conservation-biology"},{"seq":2,"slug":"restoration-ecology","title":"恢复生态学","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/applied-ecology/restoration-ecology"},{"seq":3,"slug":"climate-change-impacts","title":"气候变化生态效应","url":"/h/biology-life-science/ecology/applied-ecology/climate-change-impacts"}]}]}